comments.body:
@dlanov, the scope of #27708 has been updated to cover both unpaced traffic-generation paths in `EverflowPolicerTest`.

The current PR addresses the burst in `checkOriginalFlow()`, but `checkMirroredFlow()` still has an unpaced CBS-absorption burst followed by a sustained tight send loop. The latter can exhaust the PTF transmit buffer and raise `OSError: [Errno 105] No buffer space available` before TX/RX PPS validation completes.

Could you please extend this fix to pace both sends in `checkMirroredFlow()` as well? The paced transmit rate should remain safely above `max_rx_pps` so the policer validation stays meaningful. With only the current `checkOriginalFlow()` change, #27708 would be partially fixed.
